\doTocEntry\tocsection{4.4}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-590004.4}{QQ2-1-67}{System Description}}{11}\relax 
\doTocEntry\toclof{4.1}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-59001r1}{}{\ignorespaces System architecture of RP. The Next.js server is the single business-logic layer, with multi-tenant isolation enforced at the data layer via \texttt  {companyId} on every row. Three optimisation engines run as subprocesses, each receiving a problem on stdin and returning a solution on stdout.}}{figure}\relax 
\doTocEntry\tocsection{4.5}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-600004.5}{QQ2-1-69}{Optimisation Algorithm}}{15}\relax 
\doTocEntry\toclot{4.3}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-60001r3}{}{\ignorespaces Hard constraints (HC-01 through HC-06). A plan that violates any of these is not a feasible plan.}}{table}\relax 
\doTocEntry\toclot{4.4}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-60002r4}{}{\ignorespaces Soft constraints (SC-01 through SC-05). Each carries a per-company weight that flows into the CP-SAT objective function and the Timefold scoring function, so the same engines produce different plans for different companies without code changes.}}{table}\relax 
\doTocEntry\toclot{4.5}{\csname a:TocLink\endcsname{1}{x1-60003r5}{}{\ignorespaces Multi-engine benchmark, reference run dated 2026-05-02. All engines run with a sixty-second time budget, the same constraint configuration, and the same problem JSON. Each (engine, dataset) pairing is executed once; figures are single-sample. Wall-clock figures for small and medium were not recorded individually, but all engines completed within the time budget on those datasets. Auto picks greedy on every dataset because greedy has the smallest hard-tier penalty.}}{table}\relax 
